{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, I checked printer BL-PR-FL1. It's online and has no errors, and your laptop looks fine too, so the problem is probably stuck jobs in your laptop's print queue. Here's how to clear them:\n1. Open Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners, select BL-PR-FL1, click 'Open print queue', and cancel all the documents.\n2. Restart your laptop. This also restarts the service that sends jobs to the printer.\n3. Print a test page.\nIf it still doesn't print, remove BL-PR-FL1 from Printers & scanners and add it again: click 'Add device', or choose 'Add manually' and type BL-PR-FL1. Make sure you're in the office or on VPN when you do this. If that still doesn't work, just reply to this ticket and we'll take it further.",
  "internal_note": "P3 printing. The ticket sender is Aisha Khan (user 5), laptop BL-LT-0105. Printer BL-PR-FL1 is online and showing no warnings. Her laptop is online with 47% disk free and no warnings. Only this user is affected, so per KB-023 this is likely a local queue/spooler problem. I sent her the steps to cancel jobs, restart and print a test page, with re-adding the printer (KB-024) as the fallback. None of the escalation criteria apply. No action tools were used. If she reopens after re-adding the printer, consider escalating.",
